      "text": "489,501.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **954** and **379**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nUse the distributive property to simplify the multiplication:\n\\[\n954 \\times 379 = 954 \\times (300 + 70 + 9)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part Separately\n\n1. **Multiply by 300:**\n\\[\n954 \\times 300 = 286,\\!200\n\\]\n\n2. **Multiply by 70:**\n\\[\n954 \\times 70 = 66,\\!780\n\\]\n\n3. **Multiply by 9:**\n\\[\n954 \\times 9 = 8,\\!586\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Results Together\n\\[\n286,\\!200 + 66,\\!780 + 8,\\!586 = 361,\\!566\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{361,\\!566}\n\\]",
