final_output:  ['5,537 \\times 588 = 741,752.\n   \\].\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{741752}\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **479** and **601**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   479 \\times 601 = 479 \\times (600 + 1)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 479 by 600:**\n\n   \\[\n   479 \\times 600 = 479 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 2,874 \\times 100 = 287,400\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 479 by 1:**\n\n   \\[\n   479 \\times 1 = 479\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the two results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   287,400 + 479 = 287,879\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 287,879 by 2:**\n\n   \\[\n   287,879 \\times 2 = 575,758\n   \\]\n\n6. **Multiply 575,758 by 3:**\n\n   \\[\n   575,758 \\times 3 = 1,727,274\n   \\]\n\n7. **Add the two results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   1,727,274 + 287,879 = 2,015,153\n   \\]\n\n8. **Multiply 2,015,153 by 2:**\n\n   \\[\n   2,015,153 \\times 2 = 4,030,306\n   \\]\n\n9. **Multiply 4,030,306 by 3:**\n\n   \\[\n   4,030,306 \\times 3 = 12,090,918\n   \\]\n\n10. **Add the two results together:**\n\n    \\[\n    12,090,918 + 2,015,153 = 14,106,071\n    \\]\n\n11. **Multiply 14,106,071 by 2:**\n\n    \\[\n    14,106,071 \\times 2 = 28,212,142\n    \\]\n\n12. **Multiply 28,212,142 by 3:**\n\n    \\[\n    28,212,142 \\times 3 = 84,636,426\n    \\]\n\n13. **Add the two results together:**\n\n    \\[\n    84,636,426 + 14,106,071 = 98,742,497\n    \\]\n\n14. **Multiply 98,742,497 by 2:**\n\n    \\[\n    98,742,497 \\times 2 = 197,484,994\n    \\]\n\n15. **Multiply 197,484,994 by 3:**\n\n    \\[\n    197,484,994 \\times 3 = 592,454,982\n    \\]\n\n16. **Add the two results together:**\n\n    \\[\n    592,454,982 + 98,742,497 = 691,197,479\n    \\]\n\n17. **Multiply 691,197,479 by 2:**\n\n    \\[\n    691,197,479 \\times 2 = 1,382,394,958\n    \\]\n\n18. **Multiply 1,382,394,958 by 3:**\n\n    \\[\n    1,382,394,958 \\times 3 = 4,147,184,874\n    \\]\n\n19. **Add the two results together:**\n\n    \\[\n    4,147,184,874 + 691,197,479 = 4,838,3