final_output:  ['506,368.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **331** and **643**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number as the sum of its place values.\n\n\\[\n331 = 300 + 30 + 1\n\\]\n\\[\n643 = 600 + 40 + 3\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n\n\\[\n331 \\times 643 = (300 + 30 + 1) \\times (600 + 40 + 3)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 300 \\times 600 + 300 \\times 40 + 300 \\times 3 + 30 \\times 600 + 30 \\times 40 + 30 \\times 3 + 1 \\times 600 + 1 \\times 40 + 1 \\times 3\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **\\(300 \\times 600 = 180,\\!000\\)**\n2. **\\(300 \\times 40 = 12,\\!000\\)**\n3. **\\(300 \\times 3 = 900\\)**\n4. **\\(30 \\times 600 = 18,\\!000\\)**\n5. **\\(30 \\times 40 = 1,\\!200\\)**\n6. **\\(30 \\times 3 = 90\\)**\n7. **\\(1 \\times 600 = 600\\)**\n8. **\\(1 \\times 40 = 40\\)**\n9. **\\(1 \\times 3 = 3\\)**\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Products Together\n\n\\[\n180,\\!000 + 12,\\!000 + 900 + 18,\\!000 + 1,\\!200 + 90 + 600 + 40 + 3 = 212,\\!933\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{212,\\!933}\n\\]', '']
