      "index": 0,
      "text": "942 \\times 117 + 942 \\times 31 + 942 \\times 6 = 107,346 + 29,102 + 5,652 = 141,000.\n\\].\n\n### Step 7: Combine All the Parts.\n\\[. 942 \\times 117 = 107,346.\n\\].\n\\[. 942 \\times 31 = 29,102.\n\\].\n\\[. 942 \\times 6 = 5,652.\n\\].\n\\[. Adding them up: 107,346 + 29,102 + 5,652 = 141,000.\n\\].\n\n### Step 8: Final Answer.\n\\[. \\boxed{141000}.\n\\].\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **996** and **840**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can break down the multiplication to make it simpler:\n\n\\[\n996 \\times 840 = (1000 - 4) \\times 840\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Distribute the Multiplication\nApply the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n= 1000 \\times 840 - 4 \\times 840\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part Separately\n1. **Multiply by 1000:**\n   \\[\n   1000 \\times 840 = 840,000\n   \\]\n2. **Multiply by 4:**\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 840 = 3,360\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Subtract the Two Results\n\\[\n840,000 - 3,360 = 836,640\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{836640}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
  ],
