      "text": "68,540.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **765** and **999**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, let's break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts.\n\n\\[\n765 \\times 999 = 765 \\times (1000 - 1)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Distribute the Multiplication\nUse the distributive property to simplify the calculation.\n\n\\[\n765 \\times 1000 - 765 \\times 1\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Perform the Calculations\n1. Multiply **765** by **1000**:\n   \\[\n   765 \\times 1000 = 765,\\!000\n   \\]\n   \n2. Multiply **765** by **1**:\n   \\[\n   765 \\times 1 = 765\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Subtract the Results\nSubtract the second product from the first.\n\n\\[\n765,\\!000 - 765 = 764,\\!235\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{764,\\!235}\n\\]",
