      "text": "153,646.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Break Down the Numbers:**\n   - **500** can be expressed as **500 = 602 - 106**.\n   - **106** can be expressed as **106 = 211 - 105**.\n\n2. **Substitute the Expressions into the Original Equation:**\n   \\[.\n   500 \\times 106 = (602 - 106) \\times (211 - 105) \\.\n   \\]\n\n3. **Expand the Product Using the Distributive Property:**\n   \\[.\n   (602 - 106) \\times (211 - 105) = 602 \\times 211 - 602 \\times 105 - 106 \\times 211 + 106 \\times 105 \\.\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate Each Term Separately:**\n   - **602 \u00d7 211 = 127,022**\n   - **602 \u00d7 105 = 63,210**\n   - **106 \u00d7 211 = 22,326**\n   - **106 \u00d7 105 = 11,130**\n\n5. **Combine the Results:**\n   \\[.\n   127,022 - 63,210 - 22,326 + 11,130 = 52,616 \\.\n   \\]\n\n6. **Final Answer:**\n   \\[.\n   \\boxed{52,616}\n   \\.\n   \\]\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **250** and **327**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Numbers:**\n   - **250** can be expressed as **250 = 200 + 50**.\n   - **327** can be expressed as **327 = 300 + 27**.\n\n2. **Use the Distributive Property:**\n   \\[\n   250 \\times 327 = (200 + 50) \\times (300 + 27)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 200 \\times 300 + 200 \\times 27 + 50 \\times 300 + 50 \\times 27\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate Each Term Separately:**\n   - **200 \u00d7 300 = 60,000**\n   - **200 \u00d7 27 = 5,400**\n   - **50 \u00d7 300 = 15,000**\n   - **50 \u00d7 27 = 1,350**\n\n4. **Combine the Results:**\n   \\[\n   60,000 + 5,400 + 15,000 + 1,350 = 81,750\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{81,\\!750}\n   \\]",
