]\n\nNow, add all these together:\n\\[\n802 + 16,040 + 240,600 = 257,442\n\\]\n\nHmm, I'm getting the same result. But I think I might have made a mistake because when I multiply 800 by 300, it's 240,000, and adding the rest should give me a bit more. Let me verify with another method, maybe the expanded form.\n\nLet's break down 802 and 321 into their place values.\n\n802 can be written as 800 + 2.\n\n321 can be written as 300 + 20 + 1.\n\nNow, multiply each part:\n\n1. 800 \u00d7 300 = 240,000\n2. 800 \u00d7 20 = 16,000\n3. 800 \u00d7 1 = 800\n4. 2 \u00d7 300 = 600\n5. 2 \u00d7 20 = 40\n6. 2 \u00d7 1 = 2\n\nNow, add all these products together:\n\\[\n240,000 + 16,000 + 800 + 600 + 40 + 2\n\\]\n\nLet's add them step by step:\n\n- 240,000 + 16,000 = 256,000\n- 256,000 + 800 = 256,800\n- 256,800 + 600 = 257,400\n- 257,400 + 40 = 257,440\n- 257,440 + 2 = 257,442\n\nOkay, so I'm consistently getting 257,442. But wait, the initial problem was to find the product of 802 and 321, and I'm getting 257,442. Let me check if that's correct by using another method, maybe the lattice method or another multiplication technique.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the calculator to verify, but since I'm supposed to do this manually, let me try another approach.\n\nLet me write it vertically:\n\n```\n    802\n  \u00d7 321\n  -------\n```\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n- Multiply 802 by 1: 802\n- Multiply 802 by 2 (tens place): 16,040\n- Multiply 802 by 3 (hundreds place): 240,600\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n802 + 16,040 = 16,842\n\n16,842 + 240,600 = 257,442\n\nSame result again. Maybe I was confused earlier because I thought the answer was different, but it seems consistent.\n\nWait, but in the initial problem, the user wrote:\n\n\"Question: What is the Product of 802 and 321?\n\nOkay, so I need to calculate 802 multiplied by 321. Hmm, that's a three-digit by three-digit multiplication. I think I can do this using the standard algorithm, but maybe breaking it down into smaller parts will make