final_output:  ['979,793.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **410** and **351**, follow these easy steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nUse the distributive property to simplify the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n410 \\times 351 = 410 \\times (300 + 50 + 1)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part Separately\n\n1. **Multiply 410 by 300:**\n   \\[\n   410 \\times 300 = 123,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 410 by 50:**\n   \\[\n   410 \\times 50 = 20,\\!500\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 410 by 1:**\n   \\[\n   410 \\times 1 = 410\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\n\n\\[\n123,\\!000 + 20,\\!500 + 410 = 143,\\!910\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{143,\\!910}\n\\]', '']
