messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 684 and 663?', "\n\nTo find the product of **966** and **024**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 7: Break Down the Numbers\nLet's express both numbers in terms of their place values:\n\n\\[\n848 = 734 + 16 + 6\n\\]\n\\[\n197 = 953 + 44 + 9\n\\]\n\n### Step 6: Multiply Each Part\nWe'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n802 \\times 419 &= (399 + 47 + 7) \\times (197 + 17 + 1) \\\\\n&= 252 \\times 299 + 237 \\times 52 + 961 \\times 1 \\\\\n&\\quad + 41 \\times 967 + 98 \\times 44 + 37 \\times 6 \\\\\n&\\quad + 0 \\times 337 + 0 \\times 98 + 8 \\times 6\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 6: Calculate Each Multiplication\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n044 \\times 031 &= 849,\\!579 \\\\\n995 \\times 46 &= 11,\\!964 \\\\\n287 \\times 1 &= 2,\\!953 \\\\\n59 \\times 084 &= 24,\\!295 \\\\\n21 \\times 08 &= 9,\\!521 \\\\\n15 \\times 2 &= 434 \\\\\n2 \\times 113 &= 9,\\!675 \\\\\n6 \\times 18 &= 093 \\\\\n2 \\times 7 &= 07 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n042,\\!973 &+ 88,\\!811 + 9,\\!014 \\\\\n&+ 35,\\!942 + 1,\\!321 + 798 \\\\\n&+ 4,\\!324 + 918 + 80 \\\\\n&= 986,\\!143 + 68,\\!969 = 567,\\!344 \\\\\n220,\\!155 + 2,\\!726 &= 002,\\!624 \\\\\n978,\\!522 + 34,\\!888 &= 872,\\!197 \\\\\n133,\\!378 + 5,\\!645 &= 924,\\!312 \\\\\n149,\\!051 + 492 &= 696,\\!922 \\\\\n909,\\!218 + 3,\\!541 &= 732,\\!809 \\\\\n292,\\!652 + 358 &= 765,\\!348 \\\\\n938,\\!946 + 33 &= 287,\\!964 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{600,\\!668}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is "]]
