final_output:  ['281,633.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **268** and **314**, follow these easy steps:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Multiplication\n\nWe can break down the multiplication using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n268 \\times 314 = 268 \\times (300 + 14) = 268 \\times 300 + 268 \\times 14\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 268 by 300\n\n\\[\n268 \\times 300 = 80,\\!400\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 268 by 14\n\n\\[\n268 \\times 14 = 3,\\!752\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Add the Two Products Together\n\n\\[\n80,\\!400 + 3,\\!752 = 84,\\!152\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{84,\\!152}\n\\]', '']
