      "text": "199,546.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **465** and **524**, follow these easy steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nUse the distributive property to simplify the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n465 \\times 524 = (400 + 60 + 5) \\times (500 + 20 + 4)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nCalculate each part of the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n400 \\times 500 = 200,\\!000\n\\]\n\\[\n400 \\times 20 = 8,\\!000\n\\]\n\\[\n400 \\times 4 = 1,\\!600\n\\]\n\\[\n60 \\times 500 = 30,\\!000\n\\]\n\\[\n60 \\times 20 = 1,\\!200\n\\]\n\\[\n60 \\times 4 = 240\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\times 500 = 2,\\!500\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\times 20 = 100\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\times 4 = 20\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\nSum all the individual products:\n\n\\[\n200,\\!000 + 8,\\!000 + 1,\\!600 + 30,\\!000 + 1,\\!200 + 240 + 2,\\!500 + 100 + 20 = 243,\\!660\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{243,\\!660}\n\\]",
