      "text": "451,034.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **789** and **172**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution:\n\n1. **Break Down the Multiplication:**\n   \n   We can use the distributive property to simplify the multiplication:\n   \n   \\[\n   789 \\times 172 = 789 \\times (100 + 70 + 2)\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply Each Part:**\n   \n   - **Multiply by 100:**\n     \\[\n     789 \\times 100 = 78,\\!900\n     \\]\n     \n   - **Multiply by 70:**\n     \\[\n     789 \\times 70 = 55,\\!230\n     \\]\n     \n   - **Multiply by 2:**\n     \\[\n     789 \\times 2 = 1,\\!578\n     \\]\n     \n3. **Add the Results:**\n   \n   Now, add all the partial products together:\n   \n   \\[\n   78,\\!900 + 55,\\!230 + 1,\\!578 = 135,\\!708\n   \\]\n   \n4. **Final Answer:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\boxed{135,\\!708}\n   \\]",
